## Document Highlights

### Controllers/STM32.md
- Architecture, memory map (Flash sectors, SRAM regions, CCM)
- Clock system (HSI 16 MHz config used in MOT), timer clock rules
- Boot process (vector table → startup.s → SystemInit → main)
- NVIC priorities and ISR→callback flow
- GPIO, UART, ADC+DMA, Timer/PWM — all with MOT-specific examples
- HAL library architecture, MSP callbacks, CubeMX code generation
- FreeRTOS: CMSIS-RTOS v2 wrapper, task model, SysTick, context switching
- Linker script sections

### Firmware/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/FIRMWARE_GUIDE.md
- Complete GPIO pin map (14 outputs, 17 inputs, 4 analog, 8 PWM, 6 UART)
- Code architecture with mermaid dependency diagram
- All global variables and constants documented
- Full initialization sequence (15 steps in order)
- ISR callbacks: ADC DMA complete, UART5 byte-by-byte reception
- 8 helper functions explained child-before-parent
- 3 task analyses with mermaid flow diagrams
- All 7 UART commands (0x51, 0x61–0x66) with frame formats
- Data flow and shared variable access analysis

### Firmware/MOT-CONTROLLER-CARD/REAL_TIME_EXAMPLES.md
- **Example 1:** GET_SENSE_DATA — full UART→ISR→Queue→Task→CRC→TX trace (~9.4 ms)
- **Example 2:** SET_PWM — intensity mapping, CCR register write, PWM waveform change
- **Example 3:** GET_GAS_STATUS — GPIO alarm states, buzzer activation
- **Example 4:** SET_CURTAIN — motor relay interlock, manual/UART mode switching
- **Example 5:** ADC→Climate Control — DMA→semaphore→filter→hysteresis→relay cycle

